{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qc8GV5QvCzjLhyDWvgtjZF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Local maintenance\n2\t\n3\tRegistry audit records and host journal entries are separate bounded queues.\n4\tThe registry admits and authenticates each call even when a session handle was\n5\talready authenticated. An expired, disabled or closed handle must be reopened\n6\twith a current credential. No API changes the credential associated with a handle.\n7\tUnknown request fields outside the packet schema are rejected.\n8\t\n9\tLocal host session limits do not establish a production network rate limit.\n10\tThere is no external transport, durable journal, access-log collector or human\n11\treview interface in this package. Generic error replies suppress internal exception\n12\tmessages. A completed operation may remain effective if a caller loses its reply;\n13\tthe application's documented retry or review semantics govern repetition.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6f7856c-1cc2-4d18-a609-d259fa24c3ca","uuid":"455cd9a7-392d-41d4-adad-5a3b1ac58789","timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:23:18.537Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-review-gfi98rlo/repo/docs/maintenance.md","content":"# Local maintenance\n\nRegistry audit records and host journal entries are separate bounded queues.\nThe registry admits and authenticates each call even when a session handle was\nalready authenticated. An expired, disabled or closed handle must be reopened\nwith a current credential. No API changes the credential associated with a handle.\nUnknown request fields outside the packet schema are rejected.\n\nLocal host session limits do not establish a production network rate limit.\nThere is no external transport, durable journal, access-log collector or human\nreview interface in this package. Generic error replies suppress internal exception\nmessages. A completed operation may remain effective if a caller loses its reply;\nthe application's documented retry or review semantics govern repetition.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qc8GV5QvCzjLhyDWvgtjZF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
